bic_trace_step.reason:
The function `setup_nic_devices` introduced in this commit contains the vulnerable post-decrement loop `while (i--)` in its error cleanup path: 

c
	while (i--) {
		dev_err(&octeon_dev->pci_dev->dev,
			"NIC ifidx:%d Setup failed\n", i);
		liquidio_destroy_nic_device(octeon_dev, i);
	}


When a failure occurs at index `i`, the loop immediately decrements `i` to `i - 1` before executing the body, skipping the cleanup of the device at the failing index `i` and causing a memory leak of the allocated `netdev` and other resources.
